  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $d_n=p_{n+1}-p_n$, where $p_n$ is the $n$th prime. Let $r(x)$ be the smallest even integer $t$ such that $d_n=t$ has no solutions for $n\\leq x$.\nIs it true that $r(x)\\to \\infty$? Or even $r(x)/\\log x \\to \\infty$?",
